WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:06.120
District 9 is an uncommonly smart sci-fi hit,
and it’s got a heck of a lot going on, especially

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:06.880
in the final act.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.600
Did you come away wondering what really happened,
or musing on what could happen next?

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.220
Not to worry, this is the ending of District
9 explained.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.320
When most films end, audiences are treated
to powerful, soft-light shots of the hero

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.550
kissing their love interest, hugging their
relatives or celebrating their great victory

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.740
over the antagonists.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.860
But District 9 has no clear-cut heroic ending.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:33.440
In fact, given how much of the story revolves
around Wikus van de Merwe slowly succumbing

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.840
to a horrible disease, if you're not paying
close attention to the ending you may end

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.180
up wondering: is Wikus even alive?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.220
Is he lying in a ditch somewhere?

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.680
Did the Nigerian mercenaries finally eat his
body for magical powers?

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.740
Well, don't worry.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.720
Wikus is very much alive at the conclusion
of the film.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.000
Unfortunately, he's also very much an alien.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.670
We know this because Wikus' wife finds a metal
flower made out of trash left on her front

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.220
doorstep, which she believes may have come
from him.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:06.580
The very next shot is an alien making another
flower, so either Wikus' wife has a secret

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.400
admirer amongst the Prawn community, or Wikus
himself is leaving her small tokens to let

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.400
her know he's okay.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.460
Common sense would suggest it’s probably
the latter.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.800
It's pretty clear that Wikus becomes a full-on
alien by the end of District 9, and you’d

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.620
be forgiven for wondering if there's any scrap
of humanity left in him at all.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:30.080
Throughout the film, Wikus slowly loses control
of himself and acts in increasingly strange,

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:30.700
alien ways.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.440
That said, the flower Wikus leaves his wife
is as good an indication as any that Wikus

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.600
still clings to at least some of his humanity.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.820
Earlier in the film, Wikus' wife explains
that he loves making her fun craft projects.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:56.360
It seems that alien Wikus still feels an urge
to let his wife know he's generally doing

00:01:56.370 --> 00:02:01.620
okay and hasn't fully lost his personality,
even if he's a little slimier than the last

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.520
time she saw him.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:07.700
If you look closely at Wikus post-transformation,
it's also clear that one of his eyes retains

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.980
its blue, human color, while the other is
green like those of the other Prawns.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:16.220
This would indicate that there’s still a
small portion of Wikus which remains human

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.740
and retains at least some of his previous
memories.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.060
He's certainly more Prawn than man, but that
doesn’t mean he’s lost all of his humanity.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.200
At the end of District 9, the Prawn named
Christopher, who fights alongside Wikus throughout

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.680
the film, ultimately escapes the planet.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.200
Thanks to Wikus' sacrifice and assistance,
Christopher is able to get his damaged command

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.680
module working and fly himself and his son
up to the recently activated mothership.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.810
Of course, one question remains: how long
will it be before Christopher is able to return

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:45.300
to Earth?

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.020
He promised to cure Wikus of his illness,
after all.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.100
How long will Wikus be forced to wait?

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.840
Earlier in the film, Christopher convinces
Wikus to help him by assuring him he can reverse

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.100
Wikus' slowly-worsening disease.

00:02:57.349 --> 00:03:00.760
But after learning about the government's
experimentation on his people, Christopher

00:03:00.771 --> 00:03:04.819
tells Wikus he needs to alert his people to
what's happening before he can dedicate the

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:08.410
necessary time and alien fuel needed to heal
Wikus.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.880
Christopher estimates it'll take him three
years to make the trip to and from his home

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:12.900
planet back to Earth.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:17.310
So Christopher will return, but it's more
than likely that Wikus will be forced to live

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.940
as a Prawn for at least three years until
then.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.180
Speaking of those human-on-Prawn experiments,
just how excited do we think alien high command

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.960
will be about Christopher's story?

00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:34.140
Even without all the brutal torture and experimentation,
aliens have been treated as second-class citizens,

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:38.200
abused and manipulated by citizens of Earth
for nearly three decades.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:42.690
We don't know much about alien culture, but
we do know they have some hugely impressive

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:47.030
technology, including powerful guns and exoskeleton
power suits.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:51.510
It's hard to imagine they don’t have a military
of some sort, and who knows what other crazy

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.200
weapons or bombs they might have on their
home planet?

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:58.940
Wikus may have slightly softened Christopher's
opinion of humans, but Christopher is still

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.180
clearly upset about what's happened to his
people.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.420
Either way, there's surely no way to explain
what's going on in District 9 that won’t

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.140
antagonize the Prawn leadership.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:12.000
And if the aliens return with any sort of
retribution on their mind, humanity is probably

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.340
completely screwed.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:19.040
One of the largest unanswered questions in
District 9 is just why the alien fuel actually

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.800
turns humans into Prawns.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:25.939
It's clear Wikus' transformation starts when
the fluid is sprayed into his face, but nobody

00:04:25.939 --> 00:04:29.129
ever figures out exactly why things go the
way they do.

00:04:29.129 --> 00:04:33.379
Even weirder, Christopher doesn't seem at
all confused when Wikus transforms.

00:04:33.379 --> 00:04:37.430
He immediately knows the fluid would do that
and seems highly confident that the medical

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.680
machines on the mothership could heal Wikus.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:44.039
"Are you you saying that you could turn this
Prawn hand into a human hand?

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.320
I mean, you can make me human again?"

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:54.420
Interestingly, it also appears that alien
fuel plays some role in healing humans, because

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:58.860
Christopher says he needs all the available
fuel to travel quickly, which is why it'll

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.360
take awhile to heal Wikus.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:05.480
The fuel brings up all kinds of possible implications
for the future of the District 9 universe.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.580
For example, could other humans accidentally
become Prawns?

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:13.060
Is there more alien technology containing
the fluid out there amongst the trash heaps?

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:17.520
Is it possible the Prawns themselves could
weaponize the fluid in such a way as to transform

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.440
all of humanity?

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:23.580
Lots of future scenarios could play out on
Earth thanks to that fluid, and most of them

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.900
don't exactly bode well for humanity.

